Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 05:24:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gateway): a turn parked on a prompt an earlier restart
 handed over is handed over at once again

With gateway.restart_turn_handoff_per_turn a restart hands a turn parked on its own clarify or approval to the next gateway at once (0131's withdraw), and the next gateway resumes the stored call, which adopts the prompt under its old id (0135). At the next restart that turn was not seen as parked: the next gateway lists a handed-over prompt as the session's (background, with the generation it read before the claim) so it stays answerable before the resume, and the adopting call raised no card, so the prompt never became the resumed execution's own. The carry then held the turn until restart_turn_carry_ceiling_seconds (1080 s in a live rollout), and with it the process handoff and every handed-off subagent of the instance, and stopped it the 0048 way: an interrupted-message notice, a restart continuation with synthetic text, a new model call and a new prompt id.

An adopted prompt is the turn's own again. take_clarify and take_approval record the adoption (prompt_handoff.adopted) and tell the turn that runs on the session (on_adopt, registered by the turn runner next to its approval notifier), which binds the listed card to the running execution (PendingControls.bind: its generation, no longer background). The parked-turn check (turn_boundary._parked_prompts) counts a pending prompt the turn's call adopted even when nothing bound it. Every restart then hands the turn over at once under the same id, however many restarts the prompt waits through, and the answer on the last gateway is applied once.
